From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:50:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: re-assert GDM long frame limit when the MTU is
 applied

airoha_fe_maccr_init() programs a 16128 byte long frame limit into
every GDM at probe time, but the NPU firmware rewrites GDM1's
REG_GDM_LEN_CFG while handling PPE_FUNC_SET_WAIT_HWNAT_INIT: it keeps
the short length and forces the long length to 1700 bytes, or 4004 when
init_info.max_packet is nonzero. airoha_npu_ppe_init() leaves
max_packet at 0, so every PPE/offload init caps GDM1 at 1700. Only GDM1
is touched.

Frames above the limit are silently discarded at GDM ingress before
they reach the QDMA, so CPU-bound jumbo traffic entering through the
DSA conduit (GDM1) is dropped even though the conduit MTU, the switch
max frame length and the QDMA scatter RX path all handle it. Setting
max_packet only raises the cap to 4004, so the kernel's limit has to be
re-asserted after the firmware has run.

Re-assert the probe-time limit from airoha_dev_set_mtu(), which runs on
ndo_open and on every MTU change for all GDM net_devices (including the
DSA conduit, whose MTU the DSA core raises whenever a user port MTU is
raised).

On boot the offload setup (and with it the firmware's HWNAT init) runs
after the net_devices are already up, so the MTU-time re-assert alone
loses the race. Also re-assert the limit right after
airoha_ppe_wait_for_npu_init() succeeds in airoha_ppe_offload_setup(),
which runs strictly after the firmware's rewrite and again on every
later offload re-init.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2136,7 +2136,12 @@
 static void airoha_dev_set_mtu(struct net_device *netdev)
 {
 	struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev = netdev_priv(netdev);
+	struct airoha_gdm_port *port = dev->port;

+	airoha_fe_rmw(dev->eth, REG_GDM_LEN_CFG(port->id),
+		      GDM_LONG_LEN_MASK,
+		      FIELD_PREP(GDM_LONG_LEN_MASK, AIROHA_MAX_RX_SIZE));
+
 	airoha_ppe_set_mtu(dev);
 	if (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev))
 		airoha_fe_rmw(dev->eth, REG_WAN_MTU0,
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1466,6 +1466,11 @@
 	if (err)
 		goto error_npu_put;
 
+	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_GDM_LEN_CFG(1),
+		      GDM_SHORT_LEN_MASK | GDM_LONG_LEN_MASK,
+		      FIELD_PREP(GDM_SHORT_LEN_MASK, 60) |
+		      FIELD_PREP(GDM_LONG_LEN_MASK, AIROHA_MAX_RX_SIZE));
+
 	ppe_num_stats_entries = airoha_ppe_get_total_num_stats_entries(ppe);
 	if (ppe_num_stats_entries > 0) {
 		err = npu->ops.ppe_init_stats(npu, ppe->foe_stats_dma,
